course: dictionary
lesson: 12916
title: Estimation: a careful guess
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An estimation is a careful guess of a number or amount. You make it without counting or measuring exactly, but you still think hard about it. «My estimation is that there are about forty sweets in the jar.» Estimation is a noun, and its plural is estimations.
explain: Estimation is also the skill of making good guesses. In maths, you use it to check an answer. 298 plus 405 is about 300 plus 400, so the answer should be close to 700. If your answer is far from that, check your working.
explain: Phrases use the same idea in different ways. «In my estimation, the match will be close» means in my opinion. «She went up in my estimation after she shared her lunch» means I now think better of her. Context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: An estimation is a careful guess, not an exact count.
fact: «A rough estimation» means a quick guess that is not exact.
fact: In science, you estimate first, then measure to check.
fact: «In my estimation» means in my opinion.
fact: «Go up in someone's estimation» means they think better of you.
exercise: «There are about forty sweets in the jar. I made an estimation without counting.» What is an estimation? | *A careful guess, made without counting exactly | An exact count of every item | A type of sweet | A kind of measuring tape
exercise: Maya says 298 plus 405 is about 700. What is she doing? | *Making an estimation by rounding | Measuring the answer with a ruler | Sharing sweets equally | Counting every number exactly
exercise: «In my estimation, Sam is a kind friend.» What does in my estimation mean? | In my pocket | In my hurry | *In my opinion | In my measurement
test: «She went up in my estimation after she shared her lunch.» What does went up in my estimation mean? | I am sorry for her | I think she is taller now | I have counted her lunch | *I think better of her now
test: Before you measure the length of the table, what should you first do in science? | *Make a rough estimation | Eat a snack | Forget the question | Measure it twice without thinking
exam: Lily makes a careful guess of how many beans are in a tub. Which word names her guess? | Decoration | Celebration | Subtraction | *Estimation
